    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0242" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20210/2009: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-03T21:00:00-03:00">November 3, 1942—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 3—8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2169. Our 2149, November 2, 1 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d213-f1"/> and 2157,
                    November 2, 10 p.m. Confirming Ford’s<anchor n="66" xml:id="d213-f2"/> telephone
                    call to Berle this evening, Embassy is sending <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> with accompanying memorandum<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d213-f3"/> to Foreign Office at 9 p.m. tonight. As suggested no
                    publicity will be given this material locally pending flash from Department. If
                    and when publicity is given it is suggested it might be preferable for stories
                    to be <pb facs="0243" n="231" xml:id="pg231"/> written in Washington and cabled
                    here under Washington dateline, we to supply full text of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> and memorandum to local offices of
                    Associated Press, United Press, and Reuters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="65" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
